    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.basics\n\n### Description\n\nHi echasnovski! Here are a list of things I believe would add a lot of value if added to the toggle_prefix in mini.basics.\n\n1. Toggling quickfix and loclist.\n2. Toggling virtual lines and virtual text. (I have seen that we can disable diagnostics entirely but most of the time, I need the diagnostics signs in sign column shown so that I can identify any errors but with virtual[lines/text] disabled to remove any noise while reading code).",
