        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> 2. Toggling virtual lines and virtual text. (I have seen that we can disable diagnostics entirely but most of the time, I need the diagnostics signs in sign column shown so that I can identify any errors but with virtual[lines/text] disabled to remove any noise while reading code).\n\nI contemplated writing a function to toggle virtual lines just last night, but that was before I discovered `virtual_text = { current_line = true }`. I hadn’t realized this was an option until I saw it in [MiniMax](https://nvim-mini.org/MiniMax/). I had previously disabled virtual lines because of the noise to your point, but this is the best of both worlds for me. I also disable underline as it’s too noisy as well and extraneous with signs IMO. \n\n",
